config RUST_X86_EARLY_PLATFORM
	bool "Rust x86-64 early platform owners"
	depends on RUST && X86_64
	default y
	help
	  Build the Rust implementations of ebda.o and platform-quirks.o.
	  Rust owns BIOS memory reservation, initial legacy platform features,
	  subarchitecture quirks and the PNPBIOS-disabled queries. Native
	  configured headers supply data layouts, constants and callee ABIs.
	  The adjacent original C sources remain available for configurations
	  without these Rust owners and are not linked when this is selected.
	  GCC_PLUGIN_LATENT_ENTROPY currently produces an explicit build error:
	  its C init-function instrumentation is not implemented by this owner.
	  Combining RUST_INLINE_HELPERS and KSTACK_ERASE currently produces an
	  explicit build error: the helper-bitcode codegen path has no Rust
	  equivalent of the original C init-only stack-depth exemption.
